Not linked into ~/.claude/skills/ by default, and /sync-config leaves it alone.

This skill does a job that happens once per repo, so carrying its trigger phrases in the
always-loaded skill list costs prompt surface in every session of every project for a job you
always know you want before you type. It is reached by argument instead:

  /dev-tools guardrails

dev-tools/ holds a symlink to this directory, so nothing needs installing by hand and nothing
needs removing afterwards. Read dev-tools/SKILL.md for the dispatch table.

Any skill directory carrying this marker is treated the same way.
